---
layout: base.njk
title: Strata — Field Notes
description: Geology field notes and teaching material, shared openly with students and the wider geology community.
---
{% set subjects = ["Mineralogy", "Sedimentology", "Hydrogeology", "Geochemistry", "Metamorphic Petrology", "Economic Geology", "Other"] %}
{% set colors = ["var(--rust)", "var(--green)", "var(--slate)"] %}

<header class="site-header">
  <h1>Strata</h1>
  <p>Field notes and teaching material, open to students and the wider geology community. New notes are added by the site owner — no coding required — and land at the top of each layer.</p>
</header>

<main class="column">
{% for subject in subjects %}
  {% set subjectNotes = collections.notes | bySubject(subject) %}
  <section class="layer{% if subjectNotes.length == 0 %} placeholder{% endif %}" style="--layer-color: {{ colors[loop.index0 % 3] }};">
    <div class="layer-head">
      <h2>{{ subject }}</h2>
      <span class="count">{{ subjectNotes.length }} note{% if subjectNotes.length != 1 %}s{% endif %}</span>
    </div>
    <ul class="notes">
      {% for note in subjectNotes %}
      <li>
        <a href="{{ note.url }}">{{ note.data.title }}</a>
        {% if note.data.date %}<span class="note-meta">{{ note.data.date | readableDate }}</span>{% endif %}
      </li>
      {% else %}
      <li><a href="#" aria-disabled="true">No notes yet</a></li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
{% endfor %}
</main>

<footer class="site-footer">
  <p>Notes are added through <a href="/admin/">the admin panel</a> by the site owner — visitors can browse and download freely, no account needed.</p>
</footer>
